   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`, which prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note. The project checks pass: both unit tests ran OK, and the line-length rule found nothing.\n\n- **Date format:** The date is the `YYYY-MM-DD` part of each note's stored timestamp, for example `2026-01-02: first`. If you want the full ISO timestamp instead, it's a one-line change.\n- **Code change:** The command is in `fieldnotes/cli.py`, and I updated the usage message to list it.\n- **Test:** The new test is `tests/test_cli.py`. It adds two notes and checks the exported output.\n- **Check setup:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, so I ran it with a fresh temp directory. The command was `NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" python tools/check.py`.",
